  "about": "Ed25519 keys as a witness key (code B) or a verification key (code D), written in qb64, that a reader must take (`ok`) or refuse: a key that is not a point on the curve, one in a non-canonical encoding, and one of small order (the identity point, say, under which a signature of R = identity and s = 0 verifies over every message) name no single signer. The core (identity-agent-core/iacrypto), login-verify and login-dart read the same cases (an_ed25519_key_is_one_point_vectors_test.go, an-ed25519-key-is-one-point.test.mjs, the Dart test of the same name).",
